## Step 3 — Present Cluster Finding (per-cluster loop; mirrors review-tests.md §2.3)

For the current file, the skill processes its clusters one at a time. No batch prompt — each cluster gets its own present-then-act cycle.

**Per cluster (in heuristic order within the file):**

```
File: <file:line>
Mutator: <kind>
Cluster: C<N>  (head M<N>; linked M<…>; enclosing function `<name>`)

Original: `<code>`
Mutated:  `<code>`

{ IF head's Likely-equivalent: borderline (from mt.md 5.2) }
Pre-pass flag: BORDERLINE
  5.2 rationale: <one-line rationale from mt.md>
  Human's classification override is the resolution.
{ ENDIF }

Problem:
  <2-3 sentence analysis — what behaviour the mutation reveals is unverified>

Why this matters:
  <one sentence — what breaks downstream if this gap is real>

Severity:        <blocking | recommended | nit>
Classification:  <real test gap | production bug>
Sub-class:       <no-coverage | new-behaviour | strengthen-assertion>   (real-test-gap only)

Fix:
  <exact code change OR test addition for the inline fix>

Recommendation:
  <one sentence — why this fix matters and how it ties to the spec>

{ IF analysis surfaced production bug(s) at file:line(s) OTHER than this cluster's mutant }
Side findings discovered:
  - <file:line>  <severity> — <one-line problem>
    Logged as D<N>; will be triaged at the end of this file batch (Step 6).
  - <file:line>  <severity> — <one-line problem>
    Logged as D<N+1>; …
{ ENDIF }
```

**Per-cluster persistence requirement:** When a Side finding is surfaced, the agent writes a new entry to `## Discoveries` in the session file with `Status: logged` BEFORE prompting the human for the cluster's action. The discovery is captured on disk regardless of how the human responds to the cluster's action menu.

