## Step 4 — Action by Severity + Classification

Action menu varies by the agent's proposed classification + severity. The human's response is acted on immediately; no batch confirm.

| Severity + Classification | Human options |
|---|---|
| **Blocking + real test gap** | `yes` (apply fix + verify) / `refine <new approach>` (human-supplied edit) / `bug <rationale>` (reclassify as production bug → push to manifest) |
| **Recommended + real test gap** | `fix-now` / `ignore <rationale>` (record + advance) / `bug <rationale>` |
| **Nit + real test gap** | `fix-now` / `ignore <rationale>` / `bug <rationale>` |
| **Production bug (any severity)** | `yes` (push to manifest as proposed) / `gap <rationale>` (reclassify → severity-driven options reappear) / `equivalent <rationale>` (reclassify → record only) |
| **Equivalent** | n/a — already handled by `mt.md` 5.3 |

`split M<id> [M<id> …]` available on any cluster → remove listed mutants; return each to the head of the unclassified queue as a single-member cluster — no re-grouping with other mutants; re-present.

**Action processing:**

- `yes` / `fix-now` (on real test gap) → run Step 5 (Inline fix process). On verified pass: record `Action: fix-now`, `Fix applied: <test path>`, `Verification: passed`. On failure after retry: see Step 5 recovery.
- `yes` (on production bug) → append a new entry to `planning/mt-fix-manifest.md` with the cluster's metadata; record `Action: bug-pushed`, `Manifest entry: MT-<YYYYMMDD>-<seq>`. Advance.
- `refine <new approach>` → human supplies an alternative edit; agent applies it in Step 5 instead of the proposed fix. Same verification.
- `ignore <rationale>` → record `Action: ignored` + rationale. Ignored mutants stay in the ratchet denominator (Step 7). Advance.
- `bug <rationale>` → flip Classification to production bug; immediately push to manifest (same as `yes` on a production bug); record rationale.
- `gap <rationale>` → flip Classification to real test gap; re-derive severity-driven options; re-prompt.
- `equivalent <rationale>` → flip Classification to equivalent mutant; record `Action: recorded` + rationale. Advance.
- `split M<id>` → return each listed mutant to the head of the unclassified queue as a single-member cluster; re-present.

