## Step 6 — Per-file Write + Advance

```
Per-cluster: write each cluster's outcome to planning/mt-session.md
immediately after its action is processed (do not batch).
  - HEAD: full classification + action + (if fix-now) Fix applied
    + Verification.
  - LINKED: `Linked to: M<head-id>` + inherited classification + action.
  - Manifest update (production bug pushes): append one entry per cluster
    with Action: bug-pushed → MT-<YYYYMMDD>-<seq>.

After EVERY cluster in the current file has been processed:

1. UPDATE the running override counters on each processed head row:
     Classification proposed/accepted, Severity proposed/accepted,
     Action proposed/accepted, Sub-class proposed/accepted.

2. **Discovery review for this file** (only if any cluster in this file
   logged discoveries to `## Discoveries`):

   Read all `## Discoveries` entries whose `Discovered during:` field
   references a cluster in the just-finished file AND `Status: logged`.

   Present:

   ```
   SIDE FINDINGS DISCOVERED IN <file>:

     D<N> — <file:line>  (from C<N>) <severity> — <one-line problem>
     D<N+1> — <file:line>  (from C<N>) <severity> — <one-line problem>

   Action options:
     push              push ALL listed as new manifest entries; mark
                       each D-ID Status: pushed; add Manifest entry
     review            walk through each individually
                       (per-D-ID prompt: push <rationale> / discard <rationale>)
     discard           preserve in archive only; mark each D-ID
                       Status: discarded; require a one-line rationale
   ```

   WAIT for the human's reply.

   - `push` → For each D-ID, append a new entry to
     `planning/mt-fix-manifest.md` with the discovery's file:line +
     severity + problem (Handoff scope refined later in bugs.md).
     Edit each D-ID's `Status: pushed` and `Manifest entry: MT-<...>`.
   - `review` → loop: present each D-ID; human types
     `push <rationale>` or `discard <rationale>`; act accordingly.
   - `discard` → prompt once for the one-line rationale; apply to all.

3. UPDATE `## Current Batch` at the top of the session file:
     Next: <next file> (<N> unclassified clusters)  (or "—" if none left)
     Progress: <N+1> of <total> files classified
       Cluster-level outcomes: fix-now <N> | ignored <N> | bugs-pushed <N>
                               equivalent (from mt.md) <N>
       Discoveries this file:  pushed <P>, discarded <D>
     Remaining files: <list>
4. Set `## Status: triage-in-progress`.
5. Emit progress (one line):

   "File <path>: <N> fix-now / <I> ignored / <B> bugs-pushed
     + <P> discoveries pushed, <D> discarded
     (<C> clusters classified; <R> remaining files)"

6. IF this was the last file → GOTO Step 7.
   ELSE → GOTO Step 1 for the next file.
```

The Current Batch pointer is the single point of truth for resume — every later conversation reads only this pointer + the named file's cluster heads, not the whole session file.

### Triage exit criteria

Every cluster head Classified (none `unclassified`); every linked member has `Linked to: M<head-id>` plus inherited Classification + Action; every real-test-gap cluster has Action ∈ {fix-now, ignored, bug-pushed}; every production-bug cluster has Action = bug-pushed (with Manifest entry); every equivalent cluster has a Rationale (recorded in `mt.md` 5.3); every `ignored` action has a Rationale; Status: triage-in-progress at all intermediate points; on Step 7 entry, Status: triage-complete.

