## Step 7 — Ratchet Verdict

### 7.1 Compute effective score

```
real_count        = count of mutants classified `real test gap` or `production bug`
                    (ignored mutants are INCLUDED — `ignore` means "noted not
                     acting", not a free pass on test quality)
equivalent_count  = count of mutants classified `equivalent mutant`
                    (only category excluded from denominator)
kills_count       = killed mutants from `## Run Results` (mutation report)

effective_score = kills_count / (kills_count + real_count)        # equivalent excluded only
```

### 7.2 Verdict

```
IF previous-session score is "none" (first session)
  → Verdict: BASELINE — first session sets the bar; no pass/fail
ELSE
  IF effective_score >= previous_session_score
    → Verdict: PASS
  ELSE
    → Verdict: FAIL
```

EMIT to the human before the Step 7.3 prompt — and before writing the
verdict to the session file (7.4):

  RATCHET VERDICT
    Effective score (this session):  <X%>
    Effective score (previous):      <X% or "—">
    Delta:                           <±X pp>
    Verdict:                         <BASELINE | PASS | FAIL>

> **Regression vs scope-diff noise.** Comparison is approximate — scopes differ session-to-session. The verdict reports the delta numerically; the human decides whether a small delta (e.g. ≤3pp) is signal or noise and whether it warrants action.

### 7.3 Re-baseline (human option)

```
HUMAN DECISION (only if Verdict: FAIL or human explicitly invokes)

  keep                  proceed with FAIL recorded
  rebaseline <one line> treat this session's effective score as the new
                        previous-session score; rationale mandatory
```

### 7.4 Write Ratchet Verdict to the session file

Populate `## Ratchet Verdict` with per-class counts, action counts (fix-now / ignored / bugs-pushed), effective score, previous-session score, delta, verdict, and re-baseline rationale (if applied).

### 7.5 Defensive sweep — unreviewed discoveries

```
READ `## Discoveries` from the session file.
FILTER for entries where `Status: logged` (not pushed, not discarded).

IF the filtered list is empty
  → Skip. Continue to Step 8.

ELSE present:
```

```
DEFENSIVE SWEEP — unreviewed discoveries from earlier conversations

These were logged during per-cluster analysis but never reviewed at the
file batch's Step 6 prompt (likely because the earlier conversation
ended between cluster classification and the Step 6 review).

  D<N> — <file:line>  (from C<N>, conversation <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM>)
    <severity> — <one-line problem>
    Re-read the originating cluster's block in the session archive if
    you need the analysis rationale.

  D<N+1> — <file:line>  (from C<N>, conversation <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM>)
    …

Action options:
  push all              push every unreviewed discovery as a new manifest entry
  push D<N> D<N+1>      push listed; discard the rest with a default rationale
  discard all           preserve in archive only; mark each Status: discarded
                        (requires a single one-line rationale applied to all)
  review                walk through each individually
```

WAIT for the human's reply. Apply the same processing as Step 6's discovery review (push appends to manifest; discard records rationale; review prompts per D-ID).

The defensive sweep is usually empty — most conversations exit cleanly at Step 6. When it isn't, this is the final chance to push a discovered bug before archive.

### Step 7 exit criteria

Effective score + Verdict (BASELINE / PASS / FAIL) recorded; re-baseline decision recorded if Verdict: FAIL; all `## Discoveries` entries have `Status: pushed` or `Status: discarded` (none `Status: logged`); Status: triage-complete.

