## Fix Manifest Convention

`planning/mt-fix-manifest.md` is a cumulative aggregator of **production bugs only**, surviving across MT sessions. Test gaps are addressed inline in Step 5 (fix-now) or recorded as ignored — they do NOT land here. Step 4 appends bug entries on `Action: bug-pushed`; `bugs.md` (in a later conversation) closes them when each bug is investigated and fixed. `mt.md` Step 1 reads it (Open-section header + per-entry metadata only) for human awareness and dedup.

### Format

```
# MT Fix Manifest

## Open

### MT-<YYYYMMDD>-<seq> — <one-line summary>
- Source session: planning/archive/mt-session-<YYYYMMDD-HHMM>.md
- Cluster head: M<head-id> at <file:line>
- Cluster members: M<head-id>, M<id>, M<id>, …
- Severity: <blocking | recommended | nit>
- Classification: production bug    (test gaps are addressed inline; only bugs land here)
- Route: bugs.md
- Handoff scope: <one line — refined when bugs.md picks up the entry>
- Status: open
- Extended by (when later sessions link to this entry):
    session <YYYYMMDD-HHMM>: + M<id>, M<id>, …  (from cluster C<N>)
    session <YYYYMMDD-HHMM>: + M<id>, …

## Closed

### MT-<YYYYMMDD>-<seq> — <one-line summary>
- (Same fields, plus:)
- Status: closed — <commit SHA or PR link>
- Closed: <YYYY-MM-DD>
```

Entry ID `MT-<YYYYMMDD>-<seq>` uses a per-day zero-padded counter starting at `01`. The skill never moves entries between Open and Closed.

