## Quick Reference

### Invocation

```
Run mutation testing using /midtempo-framework/mt-fix.md
```

Detects mode from `planning/mt-session.md` Status. Run `mt.md` first if the session hasn't been pre-triaged.

### Commands

```
{{ "test" | cmd }} <path>                     # verify inline fix-now test edit
```

### Files

```
planning/mt-session.md                          — working session (shared with mt.md)
planning/archive/mt-session-*.md                — completed sessions
planning/mt-fix-manifest.md                     — production bugs queued for bugs.md
planning/<feature>-design.md                    — developer intent (loaded by mt.md)
planning/<feature>-tests.md                     — described behaviour (loaded by mt.md)
/midtempo-framework/templates/mt-session.md     — session-file schema (authoritative)
```

### Handling per classification

| Classification     | Where the work happens                                                    |
|--------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Real test gap      | Inline test edit in-session (fix-now) verified by `{{ "test" | cmd }} <path>`, OR `ignore` (recorded; stays in ratchet denominator) |
| Production bug     | Pushed to `mt-fix-manifest.md`; addressed via `bugs.md` in a later conversation |
| Equivalent mutant  | Already recorded by `mt.md` 5.3; surfaces only via Step 4 reclassification |

### Real-test-gap sub-class

| Sub-class               | Meaning                                                | Inline-fix shape |
|-------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------|------------------|
| no-coverage             | No test exercises the mutated line                      | Add a new test   |
| new-behaviour           | Test exists; behaviour not in test manifest             | Extend manifest + add a test |
| strengthen-assertion    | Test + manifest cover behaviour; assertion too loose    | Tighten existing assertion |

### Severity → action

| Severity     | Test gap                                                           | Production bug   | Equivalent |
|--------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------|------------------|------------|
| blocking     | fix-now (mandatory; mirrors review-tests.md). Reclassify → `bug` to push to manifest if genuinely a bug. | bug-pushed (mandatory) | n/a |
| recommended  | fix-now / ignore  (human picks)                                  | bug-pushed       | n/a |
| nit          | fix-now / ignore  (human picks)                                  | bug-pushed       | n/a |

`ignore` is hidden for blocking test gaps (use `bug` reclassification if the finding genuinely shouldn't be a test gap). Ignored mutants **stay in the ratchet denominator** — `ignore` is "noted not acting", not a free pass.

### Severity-prior heuristic

See `mt.md` §Severity-prior Heuristic (authoritative). Briefly: `mutator-weight + path-weight`, sorted descending. `mt.md` 5.5 computes and writes the prior per cluster head; this skill consumes it for file-batch ordering.

### State transitions handled by mt-fix.md

```
ready-for-triage      → triage-in-progress (first classification)
triage-in-progress    → triage-complete (all clusters classified + Step 7 verdict)
triage-complete       → archived (Step 8 archive)

Out-of-range statuses (fresh-start / kickoff / running / captured):
  → Entry Gate redirects human to mt.md (one line) and STOPs.
```

### Triage flow

```
Step 1   Resume to next file with unclassified clusters → silent
Step 2   Per-cluster analysis (cached file-section reads)    → silent
Step 3   Present cluster finding (per-cluster loop; flag any borderline-from-mt.md)
         + Side findings discovered (logged to ## Discoveries before prompt)
Step 4   Action by severity + classification:
           blocking gap   → yes / refine / bug
           rec/nit gap    → fix-now / ignore / bug
           production bug → yes (push to manifest) / gap / equivalent
Step 5   Inline fix process (Action: fix-now or refine) → {{ "test" | cmd }} <path>
Step 6   Per-file write + advance:
           - Cluster outcomes persisted
           - Discovery review (push / review / discard) for this file's discoveries
           - progress: "File <path>: N fix-now / I ignored / B bugs-pushed
                       + P discoveries pushed, D discarded"
Step 7   Ratchet verdict (after every file batch classified)
  7.5    Defensive sweep — push/discard any `Status: logged` discoveries
         from earlier conversations that missed their Step 6 review
Step 8   All Complete output + archive
```

### Production-code Iron Law

This skill never edits production code. Production-bug findings push to the fix manifest; addressing them later runs `bugs.md`, which enforces TDD / testing / bugs / completion. Test code may be edited inline via `fix-now`, mirroring `review-tests.md` Step 2.

